course: dictionary
lesson: 3456
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around the word and ask: what is the topic here? In a health lesson about smoking, a word means one thing. In a story about an old school, it may mean something else.
explain: «"Fags" is British slang for cigarettes, and a nicotine patch gives the body a little nicotine without the smoke to make quitting easier.» The clues are nicotine, smoke and quitting. They point to cigarettes, so that is the meaning here.
explain: In everyday talk, a fag can also be a boring or tiring job, as in "what a fag!" One meaning is a hateful slur against gay men. It is offensive, so never use it, and if you hear it used to hurt someone, tell a trusted adult.
fact: Fag is British slang for a cigarette, so it is an informal word.
fact: Fag can also mean a boring or tiring job, as in "what a fag!"
fact: Long ago, at some old boarding schools, a fag was a younger boy who did jobs for an older one.
fact: One meaning of fag is a hateful slur against gay men. It is offensive, so never use it.
fact: Smoking harms your health, which is why a nicotine patch can help people stop.
exercise: «"Fags" is British slang for cigarettes, and a nicotine patch gives the body a little nicotine without the smoke to make quitting easier.» What does fag mean here? | A boring job | *A cigarette | A petrol station | A younger schoolboy who runs errands
exercise: Dad groans, "What a fag, that homework took all night!" What does fag mean here? | A cigarette | A happy holiday | *A boring or tiring job | A younger boy who runs errands
exercise: Why should we never use the hateful slur, even as a joke? | Because it is only used in old school stories | Because it is a funny word | *Because it is offensive and hurts people | Because it means very old
test: In an old school story, a fag was what? | A teacher | A cigarette | A boring job | *A younger boy who did jobs for an older boy
test: A health lesson talks about nicotine, smoke and quitting. Which meaning of fag fits best? | A boring job | *A cigarette | A school servant | A bag
exam: Which clue in «"Fags" is British slang for cigarettes, and a nicotine patch gives the body a little nicotine without the smoke to make quitting easier.» helps you find the meaning? | The word easier | *Words like nicotine, smoke and quitting | The number of letters in the word | The word British alone
